@startuml proximity-detection
title US-05: Proximity Detection - Correlation Worker writes Neo4j + publishes proximity.candidates

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Alerts
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Kafka -> Correlation : consume position event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }

Correlation -> Redis : HGETALL entity:live:*\n(fetch all current positions)
Redis --> Correlation : positions of all live entities

Correlation -> Correlation : compute pairwise distances\nflag pairs within PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES

alt two entities within threshold
  Correlation -> Neo4j : MATCH (a:Entity {id: $id_a})-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(b:Entity {id: $id_b})\nRETURN b

  note over Neo4j
    Graph absence query.
    Checks for a KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge
    between the two entity nodes.
    Single traversal - not a table scan.
  end note

  alt no KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge found
    Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge\n(see graph-update diagram for full idempotency detail)

    Correlation -> ProxKafka : publish proximity.candidates\n{ entity_a_id, entity_b_id, timestamp_ms,\n  lat, lon, distance_metres }

    note over Correlation
      Both writes happen on the same detection event.
      Neo4j edge = durable record (queried by API investigation panel).
      proximity.candidates = real-time signal to Alert Evaluator.
      Known associates are filtered here - they never reach
      proximity.candidates (ADR-014).
    end note

  else prior relationship exists
    Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge (durable record only)
    note over Correlation
      Known associate - routine proximity.
      Neo4j edge written for history.
      No proximity.candidates event published.
    end note
  end
end

== Alert Evaluator - consumes proximity.candidates ==

note over Evaluator
  Completely separate from the Correlation Worker.
  Consumes proximity.candidates events driven by Kafka.
  No Neo4j polling - known associates already filtered upstream.
end note

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ entity_a_id, entity_b_id, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, distance_metres }

Evaluator -> Alerts : publish to alerts\n{ alert_id, alert_type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  entity_a, entity_b,\n  location, distance_metres, timestamp_ms }

Alerts -> API : consume alert
API -> TSDB : INSERT INTO alerts\n( alert_id, entity_id, alert_type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  status: NEW, detected_at, payload )\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Idempotent write - safe under Kafka replay.
  alert_id = {entity_id}:UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY:{window_start_ms}
end note

note over API
  Scope filter applied per connection:
  entity position + type must match
  the operator's saved workspace scope.
end note

API --> Dashboard : push alert over WebSocket\n(scope-matched connections only)
Dashboard --> Operator : proximity alert displayed\nstatus: NEW

@enduml
